  "grammar": [
    {
      "form": "動詞[どうし]のて形[けい] · The Te-form of Verbs",
      "tag": "Formation rules for all three verb groups",
      "def": [
        "る-verbs: drop る, add て. う-verbs follow sound-based rules depending on the final syllable. Irregulars: する→して, 来[く]る→来[き]て."
      ],
      "ex": [],
      "table": {
        "head": [
          "Ending",
          "Rule",
          "Example"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "る-verb",
            "drop る + て",
            "食[た]べる→食[た]べて"
          ],
          [
            "う・つ・る",
            "→って",
            "買[か]う→買[か]って"
          ],
          [
            "む・ぶ・ぬ",
            "→んで",
            "読[よ]む→読[よ]んで"
          ],
          [
            "く",
            "→いて (exception 行[い]く→行[い]って)",
            "書[か]く→書[か]いて"
          ],
          [
            "ぐ",
            "→いで",
            "泳[およ]ぐ→泳[およ]いで"
          ],
          [
            "す",
            "→して",
            "話[はな]す→話[はな]して"
          ],
          [
            "irregular",
            "special",
            "する→して／来[く]る→来[き]て"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "form": "て形[けい]＋ください",
      "tag": "Polite requests — \"please do ~\"",
      "def": [
        "\"Please do ~.\" Attach ください directly after the て-form."
      ],
      "ex": [
        "ここに名前[なまえ]を書[か]いてください。 (Please write your name here.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "form": "二[ふた]つの動作[どうさ]を表[あらわ]す · Describing Two Activities",
      "tag": "て-form joins clauses like \"and\"",
      "def": [
        "The て-form links two or more verbs the way \"and\" does in English, describing a sequence, manner, or reason. The final verb's tense applies to the whole sentence."
      ],
      "ex": [
        "図書館[としょかん]に行[い]って、本[ほん]を借[か]ります。 (I will go to the library and check out some books.)",
        "バスに乗[の]って、会社[かいしゃ]に行[い]きます。 (I go to work by bus.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "form": "て形[けい]＋もいいです",
      "tag": "Asking/giving permission",
      "def": [
        "\"You may ~\" / \"May I ~?\" — a very common way to ask if something is allowed."
      ],
      "ex": [
        "トイレに行[い]ってもいいですか。 (May I go to the bathroom?)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "form": "て形[けい]＋はいけません",
      "tag": "Prohibition — \"must not ~\"",
      "def": [
        "\"You must not ~,\" a strong prohibition often used for rules."
      ],
      "ex": [
        "ここで写真[しゃしん]を撮[と]ってはいけません。 (You must not take pictures here.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "form": "～から",
      "tag": "Giving a reason",
      "def": [
        "から attaches to the end of the clause that explains the reason, before the main clause or as a stand-alone justification."
      ],
      "ex": [
        "バスに乗[の]りましょう。タクシーは高[たか]いですから。 (Let's go by bus. Taxis are expensive.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "form": "～ましょうか (申[もう]し出[で]) · Offering Assistance",
      "tag": "\"Shall I ~?\" — offering to help",
      "def": [
        "Beyond proposing to do something together (Lesson 5), ましょうか can also mean \"let me do it,\" offering to help someone."
      ],
      "ex": [
        "荷物[にもつ]を持[も]ちましょうか。 (Shall I carry your luggage?)"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
